  "title": {
    "en": "Your first songs"
  },
  "subtitle": {
    "en": "Six birds you can recognise by their song"
  },
  "intro": {
    "en": "Today we're doing something different: you close your eyes. On an early spring morning, Britain is full of singing birds, and most of them stay hidden in the trees. If you can recognise their songs, a walk to the shops turns into a tour of the neighbourhood.\n\nSix birds you have already met, and one new one, the Chiffchaff, which arrives in March. Each bird has a recording, and a description of what to listen for. Play each one a few times.\n\nThe quiz at the end has no photos. You hear a song, and you choose the bird: eight questions."
  },
  "words": [
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "song"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The tune of a bird, especially in spring. It is usually the male singing, to claim a territory and attract a female."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "call"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "A short sound used to keep in touch or to warn. Birds call all year round."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "phrase"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "One song from start to finish, until the bird stops for a moment."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "trill"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "A series of very fast, identical notes, like a rolling r."
      }
    }
  ],
